# Owner-only files are the ones that judge or gate a merge or a deploy (m14,
# branchLeft/workspace#2265; source list: branchLeft/workspace#2314). Every
# other path is merged on the reviewer App's approval, with no catch-all line.
# Every line below is an explicit path that exists on main: no pattern is matched
# by a word in a file name, so ordinary role work is not owner-gated by its name.
# A new gate file is added here by its path, in the pull request that adds it.

# Estate files the merge script refuses at gate 6: mail/ runs under plan credentials on push, and every credentialed plan job installs from the lockfiles and .npmrc files below.
/mail/                                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/package-lock.json                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/package-lock.json               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/package-lock.json          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.npmrc                                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/.npmrc                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/.npmrc                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The review rule itself. GitHub reads this file from .github/ first; /.github/ at the foot of this file owns the workflows and actions as well.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# CI gate scripts and their tests: ci.yml runs the scripts/ and hetzner/scripts/ checks to pass or fail.
/scripts/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/scripts/        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Guard and deploy-account files the merge script names as gates: the project guard and the guard tests of the Hetzner stacks, and the deploy account's command, its slot provisioner, their tests and the installer that puts them on a host.
/hetzner/projectGuard.ts                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/projectGuard.test.ts                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/dns.guard.test.ts                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/tenants.guard.test.ts                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/branchleft_deploy.py           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/test_branchleft_deploy.py      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/provision_deploy_slot.py       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/test_provision_deploy_slot.py  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/30-install-deploy-tooling.sh   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Named gates: the DNS cutover stop check and its test, the suite-size pin.
/hetzner/dns/zonecheck.py                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/dns/test_zonecheck.py           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/provision/test_suite_size.py    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Test runner and coverage configs: they set the coverage scope and the exclusions that skip files.
/hetzner/vitest.config.ts                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/vitest.config.ts           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Hook set and format skip rules: they decide which checks run and which files they skip.
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.prettierignore                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The Ansible lint floors are exemption files (ANS-5, ANS-6), and the harness is the gate that runs them: a role pull request does not loosen them.
/.ansible-lint                           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.yamllint                               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/harness/                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/pyproject.toml                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/requirements.in                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/requirements.txt                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/requirements.yml                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Every file CI runs as an Ansible gate: the checks (check_delivery, check_enrolment, check_pins, check_role_imports, check_role_paths), their tests, the CI-shape tests (test_ci_python_steps, test_ci_watched_paths), test_codeowners, test_lock_reader_parity and the hash-locked pip-requirements.txt the gates install from. The pin check is the gate that vouches for the locked toolchain and for the update route (ANS-4).
/ansible/checks/                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Pull-role paths are the owner's alone (owner ruling pull-roles-owner-only, branchLeft/workspace#2340, 2026-10-21). Host playbooks are not: the reviewer App may wire a listed role into one (branchLeft/workspace#2341), and the per-host role list is under /ansible/checks/ above.
# pull_trigger decides which signed commits a host applies as root, so a change to it is the owner's to review.
/ansible/roles/pull_trigger/             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# ansible_runtime installs the Ansible that runs as root. Its install program is also what the pin check loads the lock reader and the allowed marker set from, keeping no copy, so what the gate reads is decided in this directory.
/ansible/roles/ansible_runtime/          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# host_inputs is the one loader of every pulled host's private role inputs (owner ruling, option A): the values of every host pass through it as root, and a check that fails open there exposes them all, so a change to it is the owner's to review.
/ansible/roles/host_inputs/              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# The broker deploy role's sudoers task and template decide which commands the deploy user may run as root: sudoers is a safety class, so the owner reviews it.
/ansible/roles/broker_deploy/tasks/_sudoers.yml                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/roles/broker_deploy/templates/branchleft-slot.sudoers.j2  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Each host's trusted signer list is the trust anchor of the pull. An edit to a file here is the owner's merge. check_enrolment.py (R2, R3, R6, R8) fails a change that sets a protected key outside its own file. It does not judge a role edit: roles run as root. The reusable gated apply exists in branchLeft/github-workflows, but nothing here calls it, so no gate on a role edit is wired.
/ansible/trust/                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The shared set from branchLeft/standards templates/codeowners (SYNC-1), copied unchanged, in order, as the final lines of this file: GitHub applies the last matching pattern, so nothing may follow them. It covers the standards mode and ignore files, the docs-lint settings, the standards tooling pin and the floors file, and /.github/ owns the workflows, actions and dependabot settings.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/floors.tsv        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
